        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 31 at 5:10PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Strong northwesterly winds have developed across Shelikof Strait\nand the waters around southern Kodiak Island. These winds are\nresuspending ash from the 1912 Katmai-Novarupta eruption,\ncausing haze and potentially trace amounts of ash accumulation.\nThe villages of Karluk, Larsen Bay and Akhiok are most likely to\nbe impacted.\n\nThose in sensitive groups or with respiratory ailments are\nencouraged to avoid or reduce outdoor activity to avoid inhaling\nthe ash. The winds should weaken and shift brief",
